UPDATE platforms SET notes = 'The Senhance Surgical Robotic System (Asensus Surgical, 2017) is a 4-arm, 7-DOF laparoscopic platform with eye-tracking camera control and haptic feedback at the surgeon console. It is one of the few commercially available robotic surgery systems to offer haptic feedback, giving the surgeon force sensation at the master controller. Senhance uses reusable, sterilizable instrument arms and a compact patient-side cart footprint compared to earlier da Vinci generations. Source: NVIDIA Open-H-Embodiment dataset; GR00T-H surgical VLA model (NVIDIA).' WHERE slug = 'asensus-senhance';
UPDATE platforms SET notes = 'Versius (CMR Surgical, 2019) is a modular, handheld surgical robotic system designed for laparoscopic procedures. It consists of multiple independent patient-side arm carts (each 7-DOF, mimicking human arm kinematics) that can be positioned around the patient as needed, giving a small OR footprint and flexible arm configuration. The system is CE-marked and in use across European hospitals. A key design goal is cost and space efficiency compared to single-cart systems. Source: NVIDIA Open-H-Embodiment dataset; GR00T-H (NVIDIA).' WHERE slug = 'cmr-versius';
UPDATE platforms SET notes = 'The EksoNR (Ekso Bionics, 2012) is a lower-body robotic exoskeleton for rehabilitation of patients with stroke, spinal cord injury, TBI, and multiple sclerosis. It provides 4 DOF of powered assistance at the hips and knees, with gait training controlled by a physical therapist via the EksoPT software interface. FDA-cleared for rehabilitation use in hospital and clinic settings. The device tracks steps, symmetry, and provides real-time biofeedback. Battery-powered and wearable over clothing. Source: iot-sensor-telemetry dataset (HuggingFace).' WHERE slug = 'ekso-eksonr';
UPDATE platforms SET notes = 'Figure 02 (Figure AI, 2024) is a commercial bipedal humanoid designed for automotive manufacturing assembly. It has 28 total DOF (16 in the hands), a 20 kg payload, and an OpenAI-trained reasoning/VLA stack integrated into the control system. Figure 02 is deployed in BMW Group''s South Carolina plant (the first human-robot collaboration deployment of its kind). Battery-powered with ~5h runtime, 1.7m height, ~70kg. Source: UBTECH challenge2026 dataset (HuggingFace).' WHERE slug = 'figure-02';
UPDATE platforms SET notes = 'The da Vinci Surgical System (Intuitive Surgical, 2000) is the most widely deployed robotic surgery platform in the world, with multiple generations (Xi, X, SP, 5) all sharing a 4-arm, 7-DOF-per-instrument architecture with Endowrist wristed instruments and 3D-HD stereoscopic visualization. It enables minimally invasive procedures across urology, gynecology, cardiothoracic, and general surgery. The da Vinci Research Kit (dVRK, Johns Hopkins) provides an open research interface to legacy Si models. Sources: NVIDIA Open-H-Embodiment dataset; GR00T-H; Cosmos-H-Surgical-Simulator; dVRK (jhu-dvrk/saw).' WHERE slug = 'intuitive-davinci';
UPDATE platforms SET notes = 'Ottava (Johnson & Johnson / J&J MedTech, 2024) is a 4-arm, 4-DOF-per-arm robotic surgical system under development for soft-tissue minimally invasive procedures. It uses steam-autoclavable instruments and a modular cart design. The platform is part of J&J''s broader robotics strategy (following the Auris Health acquisition) and has been shown in cadaveric and pre-clinical demonstrations. Sterilization compatibility and integration with the Touch Surgery ecosystem are highlighted design features. Source: NVIDIA Open-H-Embodiment dataset; GR00T-H (NVIDIA).' WHERE slug = 'jnj-ottava';
UPDATE platforms SET notes = 'The Hugo Robotic-Assisted Surgery (RAS) System (Medtronic, 2020) is a 4-arm, 6-DOF-per-arm platform designed as a competitive alternative to da Vinci. Key differentiating features include a modular cart architecture (separate patient-side arm carts that can be configured per procedure), open instrument ecosystem, and integration with Medtronic''s Touch Surgery digital surgery platform for procedural planning and education. CE-marked and FDA-cleared for a growing set of indications. Source: NVIDIA Open-H-Embodiment dataset; GR00T-H (NVIDIA).' WHERE slug = 'medtronic-hugo';
UPDATE platforms SET notes = 'Serve Robotics RS2 (2023) is a 4-wheel autonomous sidewalk delivery robot carrying up to 15 lbs of food/groceries for 40 km on a 1500 Wh battery. It uses 6 cameras, lidar, and ML-based perception for L4 sidewalk autonomy (with remote human oversight), operates in rain and snow, and has completed millions of real-world deliveries. The RS2 is the commercial successor to the Starship-class delivery robot and is Serve Robotics'' primary deployment platform. Source: vehicle-fleet-management dataset (HuggingFace).' WHERE slug = 'serve-rs2';
UPDATE platforms SET notes = 'The Mako SmartRobotics System (Stryker, 2006) is a 1-arm, 6-DOF orthopedic surgical robot for total knee, partial knee, total hip, and spine procedures. It uses CT-based 3D pre-operative planning with haptic-guided bone cutting (the robot resists cuts outside the planned plane), providing intraoperative precision that the system claims reduces variation and improves implant alignment. Haptic feedback and CT planning are the defining features. Source: NVIDIA Open-H-Embodiment dataset.' WHERE slug = 'stryker-mako';
UPDATE platforms SET notes = 'Tesla Optimus Gen 2 (2024) is Tesla''s bipedal humanoid robot: 1.73m, 57kg, 40 DOF with 22-DOF hands, powered by the Tesla FSD SoC (the same inference hardware used in Tesla vehicles). It is designed for factory and eventually general-purpose labor, with walking at ~1 m/s and object manipulation via vision + force control. The Gen 2 iteration improved hand dexterity, walking smoothness, and battery capacity over Gen 1. Tesla has begun internal factory deployments. Source: UBTECH challenge2026 dataset (HuggingFace).' WHERE slug = 'tesla-optimus';